# component: field
# decisions: A11Y-13, A11Y-8, COL-12, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-12, FOC-3, FOC-6
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-3, FOC-6, FOC-12: the choice card's
#     `has-[>[data-slot=field]]:has-[:focus-visible]:border-ring` plus `ring-3 ring-ring/50` is
#     removed outright, and Field restates no focus chrome of its own — a text control inside it
#     owns the `:focus` border tint (FOC-3) and a checkbox, radio or switch inside it wears the
#     global `:focus-visible` outline (FOC-12). This is the card half of the same hunk the three
#     choice controls carry.
#   A11Y-8: `FieldError` gains a leading `CircleAlertIcon` (aria-hidden) and a flex row, so a field
#     error is marked by shape as well as by hue.
#   A11Y-13, COL-12: the error ink becomes `text-destructive-text`, the `destructive` family's TEXT
#     role. Upstream's `text-destructive` is the FILL, which measures under AA as ink; `Field`'s own
#     `data-[invalid=true]:text-destructive` moves to the same role.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
